# Daily consumption — every day file

Every day that is logged gets a **`## Consumption`** block. Split it into **Daily** and **Hero** when both apply.

## Daily block — always unless explicitly zero

| Category | Debit | When to skip |
|---|---|---|
| **Food** | Player + animals · spoilage-first per [food-menu.md](../government/procedures/food-menu.md) | Never skip without stating why (expedition ration pack already counted, etc.) |
| **Soap** | ~¼–½ bar class from `SOAP-Y10-1` or working bar | Only if the day is explicitly no-wash (miles-out overnight with no water) |
| **Heat / cook fuel** | `WOOD-OAK-P5` and/or `CHAR-LANE` / `CHAR-RESERVE-C` — **state kg** | **Summer band:** cooking only, no space heat · **Winter band:** hearth + cook · **Forge/kiln/retort** are hero draws, not daily |
| **Lantern / lamp** | `DEER-TALLOW-Y10-1` · wick oil · or `CHAR-LANE` trace for brazier lamp | **Skip only** when the day is full daylight and no cave/night work |

★ **"As needed" means judge the season and the day's hours — not omit the block.** Write `none` on a line when a category truly did not fire.

## Hero block — when the day burns extra stock

Craft, haul, lap, forge, kiln, smelt, retort, glass, build: **every material row** with amount · patch [inventory/resources.md](../inventory/resources.md) or the split file the row lives in.

## Patch rule — calculate each debit once

1. **Pick amounts once** in the day file `## Consumption` block — that table is the audit trail.
2. **Patch inventory once:** `new_qty = last_inventory_qty − debit` (or `+` credit). Do not re-estimate from a different starting number in the same pass.
3. **`now.md`:** only the **resulting runway** when that stock is tracked there (wood, char, lime, etc.) — **not a second calculation** and not a copy of the Consumption table.
4. **Never** state the same draw in Events prose *and* Consumption with different numbers. Events name the work; Consumption owns the kg/g.

## Low stock — remind the player

When a draw pushes a row to **runway thin** or **×0**, add a **`## Stock watch`** block at the end of the day file (2–4 lines max). Flag only what changed or crossed a threshold — do not repeat stable surpluses.

| Signal | Typical threshold |
|---|---|
| **×0** | Any ID the next hero names |
| **Runway thin** | Row already marked thin in `now.md`, or **&lt;~3 days** of typical daily/heavy draw at current rate |
| **Season gate** | Calendar band needs stock that is not in hand (e.g. lime before kiln band) |

Name the ID · remaining qty · what breaks if ignored.

## Example

```markdown
## Consumption

### Daily

| Draw | Amount | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Food** | goat milk · stew · parched | Spoilage-first |
| **`SOAP-Y10-1`** | **−~35 g** | Wash + bench |
| **`WOOD-OAK-P5`** | **−~1.1 kg** | Hearth cook + Dec warmth |
| **Lamp tallow** | **−~18 g** | Cave scout + eve bench |

### Hero

| Draw | Amount | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **`ROUGE-FINE-1`** | **−trace ~6 g** | Fine lap |
```
